  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) only reaches 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The current RNA encoder is a simple linear PCA reduction, which may underrepresent the high-dimensional single-cell data. Question: Does replacing PCA with a learned deep generative encoder (scvi_n200) improve the RNA representation and thus validation accuracy? This experiment isolates the encoder effect by keeping profile_setting=singleprofile and aggregation=None identical to config_001, changing only the RNA encoder. Why this is the best next step: With 7 experiments remaining, establishing whether a learned encoder can beat PCA is the highest-leverage question for the RNA modality (the clearly stronger signal). A positive result would justify investing remaining budget in scvi-based multimodal configs; a null/negative result would confirm PCA is sufficient and redirect effort toward multiprofile or fusion strategies. This clean single-variable comparison maximizes information gained per experiment."
}

